  "worked_solution": "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nIn the graph, we notice a point with $x=3$ and $y=2.$ We substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{k}{3} \\\\ 2\\cdot 3 & =k \\\\ 6 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse variation equation is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{x}.\n$$",
